The card is relays/cards/cld-advisor_C19_a-negative-without-a-second-computation-is-provisional.md, committed before
the work. First in the seat's order, as M29 asks, and built on main's head alone, so that it can land before the chain.

THE GATE negative-second-computation (scripts/gates/gates.py): from B1923 on, every verdict file whose verdict is
NEGATIVE is read. It fails when no entry of cites_seat names a second computation made and the verdict line
(claim_one_line) does not say PROVISIONAL; an entry that names the second computation only as owed, assigned, pending,
awaited or not yet made does not count. It fails too when the arc's FINDINGS has no heading holding the words "What the
wall teaches" (a missing page counts as one without it). Arcs before B1923 are not read. Whether the second computation
is independent is not read: that stays main's, and the rule's "Enforced by" line says so.

ITS FAILING PATHS, tests/test_negative_second_computation.py, registered in tests/GATE_CONTROLS.json: a NEGATIVE with
neither fails (the card's control), and passes with PROVISIONAL, and passes with a second computation named; four
entries naming it only as not yet made fail, one naming it made passes; a page without the section, with the words only
in passing, and no page, each fail, two pages with the heading pass; an arc below B1923, a PROVED and an OPEN are not
read, and B1923 itself is; the gate is registered with this control and passes on the record.

BEFORE: on the tree before this patch, the new tests fail, 5 of 5 (no gate).

THE RECORD: the register of practices has the gate's section (GATED in part, the rest MANUAL); the rule's "Enforced by"
line names the gate, its failing paths, and what stays by hand at every landing. No verdict file, FINDINGS page or test of
main's is changed. On the record the gate passes: no NEGATIVE verdict from B1923 on yet.

